  "articleBody": "It's easy to use the terms \"renovation\" and \"remodel\" interchangeably, but when it comes to your bathroom, there's a big difference that can impact cost, timeline, and scope. A bathroom renovation often focuses on updating the look and feel of your current space without changing the layout. Think new tiles, fresh paint, updated fixtures, or a new vanity. It's usually more cosmetic and aims to refresh the existing setup. A full bathroom remodel, on the other hand, typically involves more extensive changes, like moving walls, reconfiguring plumbing, or completely changing the layout of the room. This can involve moving the toilet, shower, or sink to a new location. If your project touches on plumbing, waterproofing, or structural elements, that's definitely leaning towards a full remodel. The cost and timeline will naturally be higher for a remodel due to the increased complexity and potential need for permits. At HH Remodeling LLC, we can help you figure out whether a renovation or a full remodel best fits your needs and budget, serving clients all over the Denver metro area, from Boulder to Colorado Springs.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}